# Settings for one environment of the DWRG platform on the droplet.
#
# Copy to /opt/dwrg/production/app.env, and again to /opt/dwrg/staging/app.env
# with staging values. Then: chmod 600 on both (dc.sh and deploy.sh refuse to
# run otherwise). The real files never go into git. Generate secrets on the
# droplet; never reuse a production secret in staging.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, no spaces around "=", no comments after a
# value. Docker Compose treats "$" as the start of a variable: wrap a value
# that contains "$" in single quotes. (openssl rand -hex 32 never makes one.)
#
# Set elsewhere, so don't set them here: NODE_ENV=production, PORT=8787,
# TZ=America/New_York and APP_VERSION (the git commit) come from the image;
# NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS comes from docker-compose.prod.yml.

# --- Which environment this file is for ----------------------------------
# production or staging. dc.sh and deploy.sh check it matches, so a copied
# production file can't run staging (or the other way round). The app reads
# it too (e.g. as the Sentry environment).
DWRG_ENV=production

# --- Public addresses -------------------------------------------------------
# The business's domain. Caddy serves app.<DOMAIN> (production) and
# staging.<DOMAIN>. Caddy reads it from production's file; keep the same
# value in staging's.
DOMAIN=example.com
# Let's Encrypt account e-mail: certificate problems are mailed here.
ACME_EMAIL=ops@example.com

# --- Database: DigitalOcean Managed PostgreSQL -----------------------------
# From the cluster's Connection Details: the VPC (private) host, this
# environment's own database and user (dwrg_production / dwrg_staging, see
# docs/runbooks/deploy.md), and sslmode=verify-full, which checks the server
# against /opt/dwrg/db-ca.crt.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://dwrg_production:CHANGE_ME@private-db-postgresql-nyc3-00000-do-user-0000000-0.k.db.ondigitalocean.com:25060/dwrg_production?sslmode=verify-full

# --- Sign-in: Better Auth -----------------------------------------------------
# Signs sessions. openssl rand -hex 32. Changing it signs everyone out.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=CHANGE_ME
# This environment's public address (https://staging.<DOMAIN> for staging).
BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://app.example.com
# Where the web app is served from; the API only accepts browser requests
# from here (CORS and auth cookies).
WEB_ORIGIN=https://app.example.com

# --- Not read by the code yet ----------------------------------------------
# Reserved names for the services in docs/03-tech-stack.md, so each
# integration lands with a name the droplet already expects. Uncomment as each
# is built; if the code picks a different name, change it here in the same
# change. Staging always gets test or sandbox credentials, never live ones.
#
# Errors (Sentry project dwrg-server, shared by the API and the worker; see
# docs/runbooks/monitoring.md). The release is APP_VERSION, the environment DWRG_ENV.
# SENTRY_DSN=
#
# Stripe (staging: test-mode keys). Card data never touches our server.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
#
# Twilio: voice, recordings, texts (staging: test credentials, a test number).
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_API_KEY_SID=
# TWILIO_API_KEY_SECRET=
# TWILIO_TWIML_APP_SID=
# TWILIO_MESSAGING_SERVICE_SID=
#
# QuickBooks Online (staging: a sandbox company, QBO_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox).
# QBO_CLIENT_ID=
# QBO_CLIENT_SECRET=
# QBO_ENVIRONMENT=production
#
# Google Maps Platform: server key (geocoding, route matrix). The browser key
# is a different, referrer-restricted key.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
#
# Claude API: reading booking notes, assignment reasons, the weekly brief.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#
# Postmark: invoices, receipts, reminders, portal links.
# POSTMARK_SERVER_TOKEN=
# POSTMARK_FROM=office@example.com
#
# DigitalOcean Spaces: photos and PDFs (one bucket per environment).
# SPACES_ENDPOINT=https://nyc3.digitaloceanspaces.com
# SPACES_REGION=nyc3
# SPACES_BUCKET=dwrg-production
# SPACES_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# SPACES_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
